---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Flow from '../../components/Flow.astro';
// TODO(Mohit): add decisions={[{ choice, why }]} and results={[...]} with real numbers:
// monthly platform cost, sources and models, dashboards and weekly users,
// questions the team could now answer, API latency before and after OpenTelemetry.
---
<CaseStudy
  slug="saas-product-analytics"
  problem="An early-stage AI product with no data stack: the team couldn't see how many people signed up, or which AI features they actually used."
>
  <p>I set up the analytics platform from scratch, on my own: ingestion from the app and its services, a warehouse, dbt models and self-serve dashboards for the product team. Signups and usage of each AI feature were tracked and reported.</p>
  <Flow
    steps={[
      { label: 'Ingest', tools: 'dlt, Estuary' },
      { label: 'Warehouse', tools: 'MotherDuck' },
      { label: 'Transform', tools: 'dbt' },
      { label: 'Orchestrate', tools: 'Kestra' },
      { label: 'Self-serve', tools: 'Metabase' },
    ]}
  />
  <p>On the application side I added OpenTelemetry monitoring, CI and Docker to the SaaS app, and mentored 15+ engineers.</p>
</CaseStudy>
